<!--
  usb_device_filter.xml — devices the app auto-launches/auto-grants on attach
  (docs/design/android-usb-host.md §2.1). A matching <usb-device> here makes the
  system AUTO-APPROVE USB permission for that device when it is plugged in
  (skipping the dialog) and route the attach Intent to RunningSurfaceActivity.

  CONSERVATIVE DEFAULT: no <usb-device> entries, so NOTHING is auto-granted —
  the runtime system USB-permission dialog (UsbHostBridge.requestPermissionBlocking)
  remains the access path for every device. This is intentional: auto-grant is
  optional UX polish and should be opt-in per known peripheral, not blanket.

  To auto-grant a known peripheral, add e.g.:
      <usb-device vendor-id="1234" product-id="5678" />
  (decimal vendor/product ids), or by class:
      <usb-device class="3" />   (3 = HID)
-->
